    "['set protocols bfd multiplier [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'bfd interval 300 min_rx 300 multiplier 3', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bfd interval 300 min_rx 300 multiplier 3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nbfd interval 300 min_rx 300 multiplier 3\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, BFD configuration is typically done at the interface level rather than globally (though global templates exist in newer IOS versions). The equivalent command combines the minimum-interval (300ms) and multiplier (3) settings from the Juniper configuration. The Cisco command specifies both the transmit interval and minimum receive interval (both set to 300ms to match Juniper's single interval setting) along with the detection multiplier of 3. This would need to be applied to each interface where BFD is enabled.\", 'trans_template': 'bfd interval 300 min_rx 300 multiplier 3'}]]": 1,
